  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_8c17d5da1795460bb71892075a8b7aeb",
      "statement": "Startup runs as an ordered set of gates — options validation, eager resolution of GitHubService and ProviderResolver, Git repository identity checks, then a bounded mirror sync — and the process only reaches app.RunAsync (which opens the listener) after all of them pass, so every misconfiguration in that chain is a failed start with no /health and no webhook endpoint.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Program.cs#L11-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:55c780b60958294912167d4df7ef03f84d978eb4acaf0f5d177a37bcbb41a099:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L27-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:04743b75adf9aacca2db0a3dab0e92cd4445e827ee28e392050812fdb3b2eaf8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1fd6ba59aca6409aac4dc3344870303f",
      "statement": "/health is a constant liveness probe: it returns \"ok\" without inspecting mirror freshness, queue depth, in-flight jobs, or whether either credential chain works, so it cannot be used as a readiness check for agent work.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Program.cs#L46-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:379756f83d225db44f89f0cf42a2a343575eadfb81b955ed74e61d3c3e132d13:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1cc43c3cf9684f908671c552a2a88c87",
      "statement": "Git.StartAsync enforces that the content root equals `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, throwing InvalidOperationException with the message \"Sebastian must run from the repository root. Content root is '<path>', git root is '<path>'.\" — which is why the host must be started from the repository root.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L40-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d49009078aab2cac66c9694db993ff8886a75772e91084583bc594cbe995a535:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f3b8662995fe479a843a436d1aa6043c",
      "statement": "The `origin` remote must exist and parse into owner/repo via RepositoryIdentity; a missing remote surfaces as \"git remote get-url origin failed: <stderr>\" from the command runner and an unparsable URL as \"Could not parse the origin remote URL.\", both at hosted-service start.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L49-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:90617c93607b384220345870cceaaa794e2f0e9e193a8b113539fbba378d93b9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/RepositoryIdentity.cs#L5-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:82c350302cab30066216bc48c98414b01e5b884abc9ae08ee86b8d0e0c61666b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_02b1eba9a7c84a6b9e621de122938358",
      "statement": "The startup mirror sync is bounded to ten seconds by a linked CancellationTokenSource and is non-fatal: SyncMainAsync catches InvalidOperationException (Warning \"Local main sync failed\") and OperationCanceledException (Debug \"Local main sync cancelled\"), so a truncated or skipped sync leaves a host that appears healthy at default log verbosity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L143-L151",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f35d3d313b00eb901d3e7e6ec45fc0f8ffce8dbc90c8c7703a14dc4a234b112:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L27-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8e54e79299ad569dfe53557e093a405a6d5eeba2d1ed1679dd9caf9dfc8bbbea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_23deffcc97194e2f87fc4d120b422dd6",
      "statement": "The same mirror guards that only warn during sync throw inside ImplementSpec.PrepareWorkspaceAsync, so a dirty local main, a non-main checkout, or local-only commits keep the host serving /health while failing every job with the guard message and no GitHub-visible signal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L78-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d58869dfb51b549f616cff81809feec46d59c0a2a5660a893cc06c0da80fd8f1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L153-L173",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81b2daf69aaa09e46e0e9a8016e58c6eb4e7737508cfe5c23914a8c00198e6ef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_67be24a8e38945d385624e5cc08b6c78",
      "statement": "Configuration is a single bound SebastianConfig tree whose property names are the configuration keys, supplied through the default ASP.NET Core builder stack (environment variables with '__' as the section separator, user secrets, or command line) because no appsettings.json, environment-specific settings file, or launchSettings.json is committed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Program.cs#L13-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e5f8f1d827151e65b50737011dd7e6d186f09579173640ef6dcd7514eb20030:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Configuration/SebastianConfig.cs#L9-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03e295679fffe161fa5079a88fd4bdc92ca0ec0575eb4ba26c7c4f626514140e:"
        }
      ]
